# nr-tui-widgets-base: wire lines for the new crate mixdog-tui-widgets (native/core/crates/mixdog-tui-widgets)

Nothing is registered and no protocol method is added: this is library code of the terminal UI. The crate has its own Cargo.toml
(written by this task); it is not a workspace member yet, so the lead adds it.

## native/core/Cargo.toml

`[workspace] members`: after `"crates/mixdog-tui-style",` add

    "crates/mixdog-tui-widgets",

`[workspace.dependencies]`: after the line `mixdog-tui-style = { path = "crates/mixdog-tui-style" }` add

    mixdog-tui-widgets = { path = "crates/mixdog-tui-widgets" }

## native/core/Cargo.lock

A new package, between `mixdog-tui-style` and `mixdog-view-model` (the version is the workspace's):

    [[package]]
    name = "mixdog-tui-widgets"
    version = "1.5.0"
    dependencies = [
     "mixdog-js",
     "mixdog-markdown-ansi",
     "mixdog-term",
     "mixdog-termtext",
     "mixdog-tui-style",
     "mixdog-view-model",
     "serde",
     "serde_json",
    ]

Every dependency is a workspace member that is already a `[workspace.dependencies]` entry (`mixdog-js`, `mixdog-markdown-ansi`,
`mixdog-term`, `mixdog-termtext`, `mixdog-tui-style`, `mixdog-view-model`) or a registry crate already in the lock (`serde`,
`serde_json`). No dependency cycle: none of them depends on the widgets. `mixdog-markdown-ansi`, `mixdog-view-model` and `serde`
are declared for the widget tasks that fill the stubs (transcript, tool cards, status, panels): this task's own files do not use
them yet, and those tasks do not own the manifest.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Nothing (the crate does not carry the workspace-hack line, as mixdog-term and mixdog-tui-style do not).

## compose_flip.rs / protocol tables / mixdog-testkit

Nothing. The crate is not a library whose replays run from a replay package, so `cfg_test_guard.rs` (LIBRARIES) does not list it; it
has no bare `#[cfg(test)]` item beyond its `mod tests` modules and no `test-support` feature.

## What could not be compiled in the workspace

cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). The crate was compiled and tested outside the workspace with rustc and
clippy-driver in D:\mixdog-build\mig\scratch-nr-tui-widgets-base (the real sources of mixdog-termtext, of mixdog-term's frame,
paint, input and testing modules and of mixdog-tui-style's theme and palette, real vte, serde_json and unicode crates from the
cargo cache, and a stand-in for mixdog-js with the four functions the crates use): 51 unit tests and the 2 tests of
tests/base_twin.rs pass (233 frame cases and 145 function cases of the recorded corpus), and `clippy -W clippy::all -D warnings` is
clean over the library, its unit tests and the twin test. The twin test needs the ambiguous-width policy on (it is on by default on
Windows); with it off the frame test prints a line and stops, because the recording was made with it on.

## For the tasks that use this crate

* The widget contract: `paint_*` draws on a `mixdog_term::paint::Painter` at `(x, y)` and returns the rows it took; a `*_rows`
  function gives the same count without painting. Keys are pure transitions that return what the owner has to do:
  * `picker::{PickerProps, PickerItem, Footer, IndexMode, paint_picker, picker_rows, effective_visible_limit}` and
    `picker::state::{PickerState, PickerAction, PickerKeyContext}` (`PickerState::new`, `sync_selection`, `sync_items`,
    `reset_confirm_focus`, `handle_key(input, key, context, now_ms)`; the owner calls `onHighlight` after a selection change and
    runs the callback the action names); `picker::layout::{clamp_label_width, clamp_meta_width, clamp_item_index,
    normalize_footer_lines, FooterInput, ...}`.
  * `palette::{PaletteProps, SlashCommand, paint_palette, PALETTE_ROWS}`.
  * `question::{Question, QuestionState, QuestionAction, answer_for, build_answers, plan_question_view, question_panel_rows,
    paint_question, question_view_rows, ...}`: `QuestionState::handle_key` returns `Submit(answers)` (the object of the tool result
    is `Answer::to_value`) or `Dismiss`; a submit leaves the state as it was, as Node does.
  * `confirm_bar::{ConfirmButton, paint_confirm_bar, confirm_bar_width, clamp_confirm_focus}`,
    `sign_in_url::{sign_in_url_layout, paint_sign_in_url, copy_url, CopyStatus, CopyMethod, is_sign_in_copy_key}` (the clipboard is
    the closure the owner gives `copy_url`), `hint_overprint::{paint_item_right_hint, clean_right_message, prompt_status_key}`.
  * `text_entry::{TextEntryProps, TextEntryDraft, paint_text_entry, text_entry_rows, text_entry_cursor, render_text_entry_value,
    window_single_line}`: the layout of the panel and the hardware cursor cell; the editing keys and `canSubmitTextEntry` belong to
    the editor (`nr-tui-editor`), which edits a `TextEntryDraft` (UTF-16 offsets).
  * `text_layout::{wrapped_text_rows, wrapped_detail_rows, caret_position, slice_visual_row_window, text_entry_reserved_rows}`: the
    wrap arithmetic of `app/text-layout.mjs` and `caretPosition` of `input-editing.mjs` that the panels reserve rows from. The
    editor task and the layout task port the rest of those two files (`prompt_content_rows`, `queued_band_rows`, vertical moves,
    cell-to-offset): they should reuse these functions instead of a second copy.
  * `Line`, `themed`, `selected_style`, `grid_color`, `runs_to_ansi`, `paint_runs` in lib.rs for the widgets that follow.
* The stubs `transcript.rs`, `tool_cards.rs`, `spinner.rs`, `statusline.rs`, `panels.rs` (+ `panels/*.rs`) hold signatures only
  (`unimplemented!` bodies, named for the task that fills them): nothing may call them before that task lands.
* The recorder `tests/recorders/record-ink-frames.mjs` is generic: a case file names a component of src/tui/components (see its
  header), `--write` records and `--check` compares. It bundles the Node code into a temporary folder beside the script, so the
  repository's node_modules must be reachable from there (it is at the checkout root); `--tree` may be the original checkout or the
  read-only copy D:/mixdog-build/mig/ref/node. `tests/recorders/gen-base-cases.mjs` writes tests/cases/base.json.
